factory_as_code_schema:
Use a small manifest, not a universal plugin model. Example (illustrative):
apiVersion: factory.dev/v1alpha1
kind: DomainFactory
metadata: {name: gtm-campaign, domain: gtm, owners: [pmm, revops], schemaVersion: 1.0.0}
spec:
  runtime: {distribution: org/factory-kernel@<sha>, digest: sha256:..., minVersion: 0.3.0}
  triggers: [{type: repo_dispatch, event: gtm.campaign.requested, schema: schemas/campaign-request.v1.json, admissionPolicy: policy/trigger.rego}]
  artifacts: [{type: CampaignSpec, schema: schemas/campaign-spec.v1.json, classification: internal}, {type: AudienceSnapshot, schema: schemas/audience.v1.json, classification: restricted}, {type: LaunchManifest, schema: schemas/launch.v1.json, classification: restricted}]
  states: [{key: RESEARCHING, kernel: RUNNING}, {key: LAUNCH_APPROVAL, kernel: WAITING_APPROVAL}, {key: RUNNING, kernel: RUNNING}, {key: ROLLED_BACK, kernel: ROLLED_BACK, terminal: true}]
  transitions: [{from: EXPERIMENT_READY, to: LAUNCH_APPROVAL, on: launch.proposed, guard: data_brand_experiment_pass}, {from: LAUNCH_APPROVAL, to: SCHEDULED, on: approval.granted, guard: exact_digest_and_suppression_fresh}]
  steps: [{id: research, uses: gtm/research@<sha>, capability: research-readonly}, {id: enrich, uses: gtm/enrich@<sha>, needs: [research], fanout: provider, join: all-or-explicit-partial, output: EnrichmentPatch}, {id: publish, uses: gtm/publish@<sha>, needs: [approval], capability: channel-publisher}]
  gates: [{id: publish, approverRoles: [brand, channel_owner], bind: [contentDigest, audienceDigest, experimentDigest, suppressionDigest, policyVersion], expires: PT24H}]
  budgets: {duration: PT6H, tokens: 200000, enrichmentRows: 5000, recipients: 0, spendUSD: 0, retries: 2}
  effects: {outbox: true, reconcile: PT15M, compensation: stop_future_and_retract_where_possible}
  evals: {offline: evals/campaign.yaml, shadowRequired: true}
  cleanup: {revokeLeases: true, deleteTransientPII: P7D, retainAudit: policy}
`additionalProperties:false`, symbolic stable keys, semver migrations and consumer contract tests are required. Domain files live in the GTM repo (`.factory/project.yaml`, `factories/`, `schemas/`, `policy/`, `brand/`, `claims/`, `evals/`, `runbooks/`, `distribution.lock`). Runtime DB/event/effect state and raw PII do not live in Git. Engineering has the same folder contract but its own issue/PR/CI/release types.
